WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.071 --> 00:00:04.054
Once upon a time, there was a miser.

2
00:00:04.055 --> 00:00:08.496
The miser loved gold, but he hated to spend it.

3
00:00:08.497 --> 00:00:13.717
He just liked looking at it and keeping it for himself.

4
00:00:13.718 --> 00:00:17.690
One day the miser decided to bury his gold.

5
00:00:17.691 --> 00:00:20.993
He dug a big hole in his garden.

6
00:00:20.994 --> 00:00:28.238
Then he carefully put his gold in the hole.

7
00:00:28.239 --> 00:00:33.674
"Gold, you are all mine!" the miser said.

8
00:00:33.675 --> 00:00:38.075
"No one except me knows where you are!"

9
00:00:38.076 --> 00:00:41.953
The miser laughed and did a funny dance.

10
00:00:41.954 --> 00:00:45.735
Every day the miser went back to his garden.

11
00:00:45.736 --> 00:00:50.840
He dug up his treasure and stared at the beautiful gold coins.

12
00:00:50.841 --> 00:00:54.842
He watched them shine in the sunlight.

13
00:00:54.843 --> 00:00:58.693
And every day the miser said the same thing.

14
00:00:58.694 --> 00:01:04.168
"Gold, no one except me knows where you are!"

15
00:01:04.169 --> 00:01:08.106
Then he laughed and did a funny dance.

16
00:01:08.107 --> 00:01:12.684
One day a thief was passing by the miser's garden.

17
00:01:12.685 --> 00:01:15.612
He heard the miser laughing.

18
00:01:15.613 --> 00:01:21.323
"Why is that miser so happy?" the thief wondered.

19
00:01:21.324 --> 00:01:23.775
He peeked over the fence.

20
00:01:23.776 --> 00:01:32.201
He saw the miser hiding his gold, saying,

21
00:01:32.202 --> 00:01:38.212
"Gold, no one except me knows where you are!"

22
00:01:38.213 --> 00:01:43.654
"Now I know where your gold is too!" the thief thought.

23
00:01:43.655 --> 00:01:48.333
He grinned greedily and rubbed his hands together.

24
00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:53.462
That night the thief returned to the garden with a shovel.

25
00:01:53.463 --> 00:01:58.226
Quickly he dug up the gold and hurried off.

26
00:01:58.227 --> 00:02:04.111
The next day the miser went to his garden.

27
00:02:04.112 --> 00:02:14.360
He dug and dug in the ground but found no gold.

28
00:02:14.361 --> 00:02:19.279
"What? No! This cannot be!" the miser shouted.

29
00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:23.081
"My gold is gone!"

30
00:02:23.082 --> 00:02:26.936
Several villagers heard the miser shouting, and came running.

31
00:02:26.937 --> 00:02:30.659
"What happened?" a woman asked.

32
00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:40.106
"My gold! Someone stole all my gold!" the miser cried.

33
00:02:40.107 --> 00:02:43.459
"Where was it?" the woman asked.

34
00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:48.953
"I buried it here in the garden," the miser explained.

35
00:02:48.954 --> 00:02:53.511
"Every day I dug it up and looked at it.

36
00:02:53.512 --> 00:02:59.956
And every day I put it right back in this hole."

37
00:02:59.957 --> 00:03:03.079
The villagers shook their heads sadly.

38
00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:06.596
They all knew the man was a miser.

39
00:03:06.597 --> 00:03:11.146
They all knew he loved gold.

40
00:03:11.147 --> 00:03:16.019
"Did you ever take any gold out?" an old man asked.

41
00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:19.003
"Did you ever spend it?"

42
00:03:19.004 --> 00:03:24.816
"Oh no! I only came to look at it," the miser said.

43
00:03:24.817 --> 00:03:29.876
"Then I buried it again."

44
00:03:29.877 --> 00:03:34.739
"So?" The old man shrugged.

45
00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:40.103
"You can still come and look at this empty hole every day.

46
00:03:40.104 --> 00:03:43.412
You didn't spend your riches.

47
00:03:43.413 --> 00:03:54.679
That's the same thing as having no riches at all!"

